.TH UV 1 "September 2026" "uv 0.12.17" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uv \- extremely fast Python package and project manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uv
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uv
is an extremely fast Python package and project manager written in Rust.
A single binary replaces pip, pip\-tools, pipx, poetry, pyenv, twine and
virtualenv, running 10\(en100x faster than the tools it stands in for.
.PP
Project configuration is read from \fBpyproject.toml\fR; uv\-specific
settings may also live in a \fBuv.toml\fR file. Resolutions are recorded
in a universal \fBuv.lock\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fICOMMAND\fR
Run a command or script in the project environment.
.TP
.B init [\fIPATH\fR]
Create a new project.
.TP
.B add \fIPACKAGE\fR...
Add dependencies to the project.
.TP
.B remove \fIPACKAGE\fR...
Remove dependencies from the project.
.TP
.B version
Read or update the project's version.
.TP
.B sync
Update the project's environment to match the lockfile.
.TP
.B lock
Update the project's lockfile.
.TP
.B export
Export the project's lockfile to an alternate format.
.TP
.B tree
Display the project's dependency tree.
.TP
.B format
Format Python code in the project.
.TP
.B check
Run checks on the project.
.TP
.B audit
Audit the project's dependencies.
.TP
.B tool
Run and install commands provided by Python packages. See also
.BR uvx (1),
which is an alias for \fBuv tool run\fR.
.TP
.B python
Manage Python versions and installations.
.TP
.B pip
Manage Python packages with a pip\-compatible interface.
.TP
.B venv [\fIPATH\fR]
Create a virtual environment.
.TP
.B build
Build Python packages into source distributions and wheels.
.TP
.B publish
Upload distributions to an index.
.TP
.B workspace
Inspect uv workspaces.
.TP
.B cache
Manage uv's cache.
.TP
.B self
Manage the uv executable. Note that self\-update is not supported for
this packaged build \(em upgrade through apt instead.
.TP
.B auth
Manage authentication for package indexes.
.TP
.B help [\fICOMMAND\fR]
Display the long\-form documentation for a command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the concise help for this command.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the uv version.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Use verbose output. Repeat for more detail.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Use quiet output. Repeat for less output.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-cache
Avoid reading from or writing to the cache, using a temporary directory
for the duration of the operation.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " CACHE_DIR"
Path to the cache directory.
.TP
.B \-\-managed\-python
Require the use of uv\-managed Python versions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-managed\-python
Disable the use of uv\-managed Python versions.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-python\-downloads
Disable automatic downloads of Python.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " WHEN"
Control the use of color in output: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR or
\fBnever\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Disable network access.
.TP
.BI \-\-directory " DIRECTORY"
Change to the given directory prior to running the command.
.TP
.BI \-\-project " PROJECT"
Discover a project in the given directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-file " CONFIG_FILE"
The path to a \fBuv.toml\fR file to use for configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Avoid discovering configuration files.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Hide all progress output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a project and add a dependency:
.PP
.RS
.B uv init mygame && cd mygame && uv add pygame
.RE
.PP
Create a virtual environment and install into it:
.PP
.RS
.B uv venv && uv pip install rich
.RE
.PP
Install a command\-line tool for the current user:
.PP
.RS
.B uv tool install shrinkray
.RE
.PP
Show which interpreter uv would use:
.PP
.RS
.B uv python find
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B pyproject.toml
Project metadata; uv settings under \fB[tool.uv]\fR.
.TP
.B uv.toml
Standalone uv configuration (same format, no \fB[tool.uv]\fR wrapper).
.TP
.B uv.lock
The project's universal lockfile.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UV_CACHE_DIR
Path to the cache directory.
.TP
.B UV_PYTHON
The Python interpreter to use by default.
.TP
.B UV_NO_CACHE
Disable the cache when set.
.TP
.B UV_OFFLINE
Disable network access when set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uvx (1),
.BR python3 (1),
.BR pip (1)
.PP
